# UI Component Rules

## Structure
```tsx
const MyComponent = React.forwardRef<View, MyComponentProps>((props, ref) => {
  const { colors } = useTheme();
  const styles = StyleSheet.create({ /* theme-driven */ });
  return <View ref={ref} style={styles.root}>{/* ... */}</View>;
});
MyComponent.displayName = "MyComponent";
export default MyComponent;
```

## Theming
- Colors: `useTheme().colors` — never hardcode `#hex` for semantic colors.
- Typography: `typography.*` from `src/lib/typography.ts` — no raw `fontSize: 14`.
- Light/dark: tokens live in `src/styles/globals.css`; do not fork palettes in components.

## UX
- Always handle `disabled`, loading, and error states where applicable.
- Touch targets ≥ 44pt height for primary controls.
- Overlays (Modal, Sheet, Drawer): support `onRequestClose`, overlay dismiss, safe areas.

## Styling
- Prefer `StyleSheet.create` over inline objects when using theme values.
- Use `platformSpecificStyles` for elevation/shadows when cross-platform parity matters.
- Accept `style` / `containerStyle` overrides on public components.

## Avoid
- Business logic, fetch calls, or navigation inside UI files.
- Web-only APIs without `typeof document !== "undefined"` guards (see theme-context).
- New color/spacing scales — use existing `spacing`, `borderRadius`, `typography`.
